The code audit has exposed a lock-state edge the new tests do not cover: failed/releasing acquisitions mutate the process registry separately from the filesystem lock. I’m running two deterministic probes now—one for a caught reentrant failure weakening the held-home invariant, and one for the release handoff between concurrent home consumers.
